# behavior: a `mut` pattern binding of a place needs a place that permits mutation; `Some(mut items)` matched on a field of a read-only `cart` is refused at the binding, whether or not the arm changes it, and never becomes a copy or a move (RFC 129 writable alias rule 8, #1846).
# pending: a pattern does not accept `mut name`; the program is refused as a syntax error, with no ownership diagnostic.
# expect-diagnostic: INCAN-T0126

class Cart:
    pub items: Option[list[str]]


def main() -> None:
    cart = Cart(items=Some(["apple"]))
    match cart.items:
        Some(mut items) => println(len(items))
        None => pass
